  "markdown_report": "### Insights and directions\n\n**Starting-point insights.** (1) Users reject broad relevance when it misses their immediate purpose; recent coherent interactions should therefore influence context selection. (2) Older, isolated purchases persist as interests, while duplicate recommendations lack evidence of renewed need; indiscriminate history aggregation deserves scrutiny, although purchase intent remains unobserved. (3) Electronics has 12.27% sampled ranking errors and a −0.2595 lower-decile margin. Embedding-collapse scores near 0.5 indicate approximately orthogonal average directions, so global decorrelation is poorly motivated.\n\n**Related-work insights.** (1) [NextItNet](https://arxiv.org/abs/1808.05163) expands causal context through dilated residual convolutions; choosing how much distant context contributes is a compatible extension. (2) [GAT4Rec](https://www.mdpi.com/2227-7390/12/14/2189/html) motivates selective context, but does not establish gains for gated NextItNet. (3) [sampled-softmax research](https://wujcan.github.io/papers/tois-ssm.pdf) motivates stronger candidate discrimination while warning that low temperatures overemphasize difficult negatives.\n\n### Framework and candidate assessment\n\nThe framework separates **context selection**, **candidate supervision**, and **item representation**. Each changes one component within a single jointly trained category model. Scores below give originality/potential/user alignment/model alignment/implementation difficulty; higher difficulty means harder implementation. Each assessment includes a benefit (+) and limitation (−).\n\n| Idea | Scores | Critical assessment by dimension |\n|---|---|---|\n| A. Gate each dilated residual update | 5/7/8/6/3 | Originality: + task-specific adaptation, − established gating. Potential: + adaptive context, − gains uncertain. User: + targets stale interests and broad mismatches, − cannot infer compatibility. Model: + may remove confusing context, − margins may remain weak. Difficulty: + small module, − padding discipline required. |\n| B. Uniform multi-negative sampled softmax | 3/7/5/8/3 | Originality: + practical adaptation, − standard objective. Potential: + stronger discrimination, − sampling-sensitive. User: + compares alternatives, − little intent modeling. Model: + targets weak margins, − false negatives possible. Difficulty: + vectorizable, − memory grows. |\n| C. Jointly learned title-token embeddings | 5/6/7/5/6 | Originality: + constrained adaptation, − established text fusion. Potential: + specific item identity, − sparse vocabulary. User: + finer distinctions, − text cannot prove fit. Model: + shares evidence, − may amplify similarity confusion. Difficulty: + no external weights, − tokenization and predictor changes. |\n\n### Selected idea: gated causal context\n\nAt 0% progress, choose **A** for a small, interpretable first experiment. A causal gate controls each existing dilated residual update using its current hidden state and proposed update. This explicitly targets **stale isolated interests** and **broad matches that obscure recent purpose**. Suppressing distracting context could also improve Electronics’ weak lower-tail separation; this remains a hypothesis.\n\nTrain one checkpoint per category using the supplied objective and fixed seeds, splits, and limits. Compare with the corrected cold start through host macro validation HR@10. Repeat measured margin diagnostics and simulator rejection assessments; claim neither compatibility recovery nor improvement before evaluation.",
  "idea": {
    "description": "Add a jointly trained, positionwise gate to each residual dilated-convolution block in the supplied NextItNet. Preserve every causal convolution and existing dilation schedule. For hidden state h and its causal residual update u, compute g = sigmoid(W[h;u] + b) and output h + g*u. Gates operate inside one network and do not combine independently fitted predictors.",
    "motivation": "The user diagnosis identifies stale isolated interactions and broad relevance displacing specific recent interests. Adaptive residual contributions may reduce these distractions while retaining useful distant evidence. Electronics' 12.27% sampled wrong-rank rate and negative tenth-percentile margin provide a model-facing target. Neither those measurements nor the proposal establishes improved validation HR@10.",
    "implementation_notes": "Implement gates with positionwise linear layers or kernel-1 convolutions; no bidirectional pooling or future inputs. Initialize gate weights to zero and bias to 2 so initial behavior stays near the supplied backbone. Retain baseline loss, optimizer, sampling, dimensions, and dilation schedule for this first comparison. Mask padding after every block. Preserve log2feats(sequence), item_emb, predict_score(features, items), family-specific sample_batch, and ModelView. Read out the maximum valid sequence index, never count-1. Update the embedded predictor writer and save architecture configuration with the checkpoint. Keep exactly one trained checkpoint per category with all four routing branches. DATA_DIR remains os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR']; artifacts remain beneath the trial directory. Use preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, at most 200 epochs and 200 batches per epoch on one GPU. Retain DiagnosisProbe(view, device), run_full_diagnosis(train_loader) returning metrics and metric_definitions, and diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis). Measure margins only on valid positions; mark metadata-category diagnostics unavailable because item categories are unavailable. Do not introduce timestamps into this first variant, so the sequence-only diagnostic interface remains sufficient. No new training or validation result is claimed.",
    "pseudocode": "class GatedNextItNet:\n    log2feats(sequence):\n        valid = sequence != 0\n        h = baseline_input_embedding(sequence) * valid[..., None]\n        for block, gate in paired_causal_blocks_and_gates:\n            u = block.residual_update(h)  # retain baseline causal convolutions\n            g = sigmoid(gate(concat(h, u, dim=-1)))\n            h = (h + g * u) * valid[..., None]\n        return baseline_output_transform(h) * valid[..., None]\n\nfor category in FOUR_REQUIRED_CATEGORIES:\n    seed_all(42)\n    model = GatedNextItNet(baseline_category_configuration)\n    for epoch in range(min(configured_epochs, 200)):\n        for batch in family_sample_batches(count=200):\n            optimize(baseline_loss(model, batch))\n        run_existing_validation_and_checkpoint_selection()\n    save_one_selected_checkpoint_and_matching_predictor_configuration()\n\npredict(sequence, candidates):\n    features = model.log2feats(sequence)\n    positions = arange(sequence_length)\n    last = where(sequence != 0, positions, -1).max(dim=-1)\n    handle_empty_histories_using_supplied_baseline_policy()\n    return model.predict_score(features[batch_indices, last], candidates)",
    "originality": {
      "score": 5,
      "positive": "Applies positionwise residual gating directly to the diagnosed context-selection problem while preserving NextItNet.",
      "negative": "Gating residual updates and selecting context are established techniques; novelty is primarily the constrained adaptation."
    },
    "future_potential": {
      "score": 7,
      "positive": "Provides a small foundation for studying whether adaptive context helps recent intent and difficult positive-negative discrimination.",
      "negative": "Gates may saturate or reproduce the baseline, and observational histories cannot identify replacement needs or product compatibility."
    },
    "code_difficulty": {
      "score": 3,
      "positive": "Requires a small module per existing residual block and no external data, retrieval index, or additional model.",
      "negative": "Causal masking, checkpoint reconstruction, and the embedded predictor must remain exactly consistent."
    }
  },
  "related_work": [
    {
      "title": "NextItNet: A Simple Convolutional Generative Network for Next Item Recommendation",
      "link": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1808.05163",
      "contributions": [
        "Establishes residual dilated causal convolutions for next-item recommendation.",
        "Supplies the backbone retained by the proposed gated residual updates."
      ],
      "limitations": [
        "Does not establish that the proposed gates improve this four-category benchmark.",
        "Next-item supervision does not identify purchase purpose or compatibility."
      ]
    },
    {
